---

import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";
import Layout from "../Layout/Layout.astro";
import Placeholder from "../assets/Charli(placeholder).jpg"

const citations = [
    {
        Inline: "1",
        mla: "LifeTouch, “Knapp Senior Photos”, 2025",
    },
    {
        Inline: "2",
        mla: "Huang, “Golfing”, 2024",
    }
]

---

<Layout title="Story" Citations={citations}>
    <div class="u-container flex flex-col content-center">
        <div class="flex-auto h-full w-full py-60 z-2 text-center">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold py-5">
                So yeah this is some text
            </h1>
            <Image src={Placeholder} alt="inline image" class="float-right h-48 w-96 object-fit right-30 inset-30"/>
            <p class="text-lg" data-sy-reveal="lines">
                So then we begin to talk about what happened. And then we'd see if there was actually image wrap or if I'm a dumbass, it's probably the second one.
                Maybe I'll even continue here, or maybe I should just copy paste the text that Charli has written...
                Turns out she hasn't actually written that section yet, so I'm left to type too many words in order to test my code.
                Maybe it'll even wrap around the image that I put. Perhaps I'll even commit a small crime. Maybe just like...
                <span class="font-bold text-red-500">Arson!!</span>
                or perhaps I'll just live in the gutters. Did I really need a single line in order to test it? <span class="text-yellow-300 font-black">Gods! </span><span class="text-red-500 font-black">damn</span> them!
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg">
                WOMP WOMP
            </p>

        </div>
        <div class="grid-span-full h-full w-full pt-50 pb-5 z-2 text-center">
            <h1 class="text-xl font-medium">
                So yeah, we did something.
            </h1>
            <p>
                So then we begin to talk about what happened. And then we'd see if there was actually image wrap or if I'm a dumbass, it's probably the second one.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>